# Line endings are pinned to LF in the working tree.
#
# Several contract tests under scripts/ assert on the literal source text of
# server/services/*.js, and some of those expectations embed "\n" (see
# check-longform-compress-lane-contract.js). A CRLF checkout — which is what
# git produces on Windows when core.autocrlf=true — makes those assertions
# fail even though the code is correct. This surfaced cloning the repo onto
# the N100 machine, where every file checked out CRLF and `npm run verify`
# failed on an untouched contract.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binary files (mp4/mp3/onnx/jpg)
# alone; only text files are normalized.
* text=auto eol=lf
